# Root image does not need development scripts or unrelated infrastructure
infra/*
!infra/martin/
!infra/martin/martin.yaml

# Only the scripts the image itself runs: the build-stage data-boundary gate
# (plus every check-*.mjs it imports) and the pre-deploy migration runner.
# The re-include is a whole-pattern one so adding a new check to
# check-data-boundaries.mjs cannot silently break the Docker build again.
#
# *.sql is re-included for the same reason, one step further along: the build
# stage runs `npm test`, and src/__tests__/lib/geometry-migration.test.ts reads
# scripts/backfill-geometry.sql to assert the backfill's dating rules. A test
# that reads a repo file passes locally and fails only inside the image, so the
# pattern is whole-suffix rather than a single filename.
scripts/*
!scripts/check-*.mjs
!scripts/migrate.mjs
!scripts/*.sql
!scripts/warm-soilgrids.mjs
